1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Once upon a time, there was a princess who was held captive.

2
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:12,080
She was imprisoned in the Demon King's castle, her freedom taken from her.

3
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:20,220
The princess had no choice but to dance like a puppet to the tune set by the whims of her sadistic captor.

4
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:25,960
One day, a hero came to fight the Demon King, seeking to save the princess.

5
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,920
However, there was no way the hero could attain the victory.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,200
For you see, the hero did not know that he himself was a puppet that the Demon King had created.

7
00:02:25,354 --> 00:02:28,354
Vakir!

8
00:02:30,354 --> 00:02:31,354
Tutu!

9
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:35,354
Where am I?

10
00:02:36,354 --> 00:02:37,354
Gears?

11
00:02:38,354 --> 00:02:39,354
Why are they all stopped?

12
00:02:40,354 --> 00:02:41,354
What am I doing?

13
00:02:42,354 --> 00:02:43,354
In a place like this?

14
00:02:44,354 --> 00:02:45,354
What should I do now?

15
00:02:46,354 --> 00:02:47,354
Vakir!

16
00:02:52,354 --> 00:02:53,354
Drosselmeyer.

17
00:02:53,354 --> 00:02:56,354
The man who toys with everyone's fates.

18
00:02:58,354 --> 00:03:03,354
Is he out there somewhere, laughing as he watches her and Muto suffer?

19
00:03:04,354 --> 00:03:05,354
Where is she right now?

20
00:03:06,354 --> 00:03:08,354
Is she where Drosselmeyer is?

21
00:03:10,354 --> 00:03:11,354
Where the hell is that?

22
00:03:12,354 --> 00:03:16,354
By now this story may have progressed to the point where we can do nothing.

23
00:03:16,354 --> 00:03:20,354
In that case, the only one who can fight is he who carries the same blood!

24
00:03:20,354 --> 00:03:22,354
You mean, I should write then?

25
00:03:22,354 --> 00:03:25,354
There's no other way that I'll be able to save her at this point.

26
00:03:30,354 --> 00:03:31,354
Where is the exit?

27
00:03:32,354 --> 00:03:33,354
I must leave this place.

28
00:03:34,354 --> 00:03:35,354
I know where they are.

29
00:03:36,354 --> 00:03:39,354
The other heart shards are in the five gates around the town.

30
00:03:39,354 --> 00:03:42,354
I must return them to Muto soon.

31
00:03:43,354 --> 00:03:46,354
And then Muto will return to the story.

32
00:03:47,354 --> 00:03:49,354
And I'll go back to being...

33
00:03:50,354 --> 00:03:51,354
A duck.

34
00:03:51,354 --> 00:03:52,354
Shhh!

35
00:03:53,354 --> 00:03:54,354
What's this?

36
00:03:54,354 --> 00:03:55,354
A puppet?

37
00:03:55,354 --> 00:03:56,354
Yes, that's right!

38
00:03:56,354 --> 00:03:58,354
You're in the puppet world now!

39
00:03:59,354 --> 00:04:00,354
Who's this?

40
00:04:00,354 --> 00:04:02,354
You're Princess Tootoo, aren't you?

41
00:04:03,354 --> 00:04:04,354
It's Tootoo!

42
00:04:04,354 --> 00:04:05,354
It's Tootoo!

43
00:04:06,354 --> 00:04:07,354
It's Tootoo!

44
00:04:07,354 --> 00:04:08,354
It's Tootoo!

45
00:04:08,354 --> 00:04:09,354
We wonder what Tootoo is tootoo!

46
00:04:09,354 --> 00:04:10,354
Do you know where this place is?

47
00:04:11,354 --> 00:04:12,354
Please tell me!

48
00:04:13,354 --> 00:04:14,354
Why was I brought here?

49
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:15,354
Was there some reason?

50
00:04:16,354 --> 00:04:18,354
Why has everything in this place just stopped?

51
00:04:19,354 --> 00:04:21,354
That's rather irresponsible of you, wouldn't you say?

52
00:04:21,354 --> 00:04:22,354
Not knowing where you are?

53
00:04:23,354 --> 00:04:24,354
Then please, tell me!

54
00:04:25,354 --> 00:04:26,354
Tootoo says she wants us to tell her!

55
00:04:27,354 --> 00:04:28,354
This is Tootoo in a pickle!

56
00:04:29,354 --> 00:04:30,354
A pickle!

57
00:04:33,354 --> 00:04:34,354
Enter me!

58
00:04:36,354 --> 00:04:38,354
You're the one who stopped everything, Princess Tootoo!

59
00:04:39,354 --> 00:04:40,354
Didn't you know?

60
00:04:40,354 --> 00:04:41,354
This is the inside of the story!

61
00:04:42,354 --> 00:04:45,354
And you're the one who caused the story to stop!

62
00:04:45,354 --> 00:04:46,354
Caused the story to stop?

63
00:04:47,354 --> 00:04:48,354
I did it?

64
00:04:48,354 --> 00:04:49,354
That's right!

65
00:04:49,354 --> 00:04:50,354
Tootoo stopped the story!

66
00:04:51,354 --> 00:04:52,354
Tootoo stopped all the gears!

67
00:04:53,354 --> 00:04:54,354
She stopped them!

68
00:04:54,354 --> 00:04:55,354
She stopped them!

69
00:04:55,354 --> 00:04:56,354
Tootoo stopped them!

70
00:04:56,354 --> 00:04:57,354
Tootoo stopped them!

71
00:04:57,354 --> 00:04:58,354
Tootoo stopped them!

72
00:04:59,354 --> 00:05:00,354
Stop it!

73
00:05:03,354 --> 00:05:04,354
My body!

74
00:05:05,354 --> 00:05:06,354
It won't move!

75
00:05:17,354 --> 00:05:19,354
Hear the voice which is voiceless,

76
00:05:19,354 --> 00:05:21,354
and see the shape which is shapeless.

77
00:05:22,354 --> 00:05:24,354
What am I supposed to do with that?

78
00:05:24,354 --> 00:05:25,354
What should I write?

79
00:05:25,354 --> 00:05:26,354
What should I write?

80
00:05:43,354 --> 00:05:44,354
Damn it!

81
00:05:44,354 --> 00:05:45,354
I have to write!

82
00:05:45,354 --> 00:05:46,354
Where is the heart?

83
00:05:46,354 --> 00:05:50,354
Daughter, hurry up and fetch me a heart!

84
00:05:50,354 --> 00:05:54,354
Dear father, now that I have gone and dyed the prince's heart in your blood, he'll definitely become mine, right father?

85
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:55,354
Are you saying you cannot trust what I tell you?

86
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:56,354
Oh no!

87
00:05:56,354 --> 00:05:57,354
Of course not!

88
00:05:57,354 --> 00:05:58,354
And you think, on top of that, you only consider yourself and not me!

89
00:05:58,354 --> 00:05:59,354
Your father?

90
00:05:59,354 --> 00:06:00,354
That's not true!

91
00:06:00,354 --> 00:06:01,354
That's not true!

92
00:06:01,354 --> 00:06:02,354
I love you, father, but...

93
00:06:02,354 --> 00:06:03,354
It's only natural for a daughter to love her father!

94
00:06:03,354 --> 00:06:04,354
It's only natural for a daughter to love her father!

95
00:06:04,354 --> 00:06:05,354
It's only natural for a daughter to love her father!

96
00:06:05,354 --> 00:06:08,354
And you think, on top of that, you only consider yourself and not me, your father!

97
00:06:08,354 --> 00:06:09,354
That's not true!

98
00:06:09,354 --> 00:06:10,354
I love you, father, but...

99
00:06:10,354 --> 00:06:32,354
It's only natural for a daughter to love her father!

100
00:06:32,354 --> 00:06:33,354
You're pathetic!

101
00:06:33,354 --> 00:06:37,874
Pathetic. To think you can't even get the love of the prince in the story.

102
00:06:38,294 --> 00:06:42,674
At this point, you no longer have any value to me as a daughter.

103
00:06:42,914 --> 00:06:43,434
Father!

104
00:06:43,954 --> 00:06:49,854
You should at least give me your heart, so that I might be restored to some degree, however small.

105
00:06:49,954 --> 00:06:52,874
Father! Forgive me, I'm sorry!

106
00:06:53,514 --> 00:06:56,834
I have not given you leave, Prey!

107
00:06:58,734 --> 00:07:01,654
Have I turned into a puppet?

108
00:07:01,654 --> 00:07:04,714
Did I do something bad? Is that why?

109
00:07:07,374 --> 00:07:08,654
Is that...

110
00:07:09,974 --> 00:07:10,534
Uzura!

111
00:07:13,454 --> 00:07:15,014
I found Tutu, Zura!

112
00:07:15,114 --> 00:07:16,734
What are you doing here, Uzura?

113
00:07:17,094 --> 00:07:19,794
I followed you, Zura. What are you doing, Zura?

114
00:07:19,994 --> 00:07:23,034
I think I've somehow turned into a puppet.

115
00:07:23,954 --> 00:07:25,214
A puppet, Zura?

116
00:07:26,034 --> 00:07:29,654
It's not that I don't like being a puppet, it's just...

117
00:07:29,654 --> 00:07:31,414
Uzura!

118
00:07:31,654 --> 00:07:40,454
A puppet, Zura?

119
00:07:43,454 --> 00:07:44,334
Uzura!

120
00:07:45,334 --> 00:07:48,074
Je t'ai entrelacé.

121
00:07:48,074 --> 00:07:52,514
My feet are moving on their own.

122
00:07:53,234 --> 00:07:55,874
Pretty long de jambes, Antoineau.

123
00:07:56,294 --> 00:08:01,614
Mr. Drosselmeyer? Is this the world where Mr. Drosselmeyer is?

124
00:08:01,614 --> 00:08:16,414
How? Why? I'm just a marionette dancing exactly as I'm told. I don't like this. I want to dance more... more freely.

125
00:08:16,414 --> 00:08:19,214
Such thinking is mistaken.

126
00:08:19,214 --> 00:08:30,214
Marionettes are their most free when they're being manipulated by their strings. You won't be able to leave this place unless you acknowledge that.

127
00:08:30,214 --> 00:08:32,014
What's a puppet, Zura?

128
00:08:32,014 --> 00:08:38,014
Well, her name is Uzura. Karin, he made her from the wood from Edel that didn't burn up.

129
00:08:38,014 --> 00:08:40,014
From Miss Edel?

130
00:08:40,014 --> 00:08:44,814
Does that mean I'm not Uzra, Zura?

131
00:08:44,814 --> 00:08:45,814
Huh?

132
00:08:45,814 --> 00:08:46,814
Oh!

133
00:08:46,814 --> 00:08:51,814
What's this, Zura?

134
00:08:51,814 --> 00:08:53,614
Oh! It hurts, Zura!

135
00:08:53,614 --> 00:08:54,614
Oh! It hurts, Zura!

136
00:08:54,614 --> 00:08:55,614
Oh!

137
00:08:55,614 --> 00:08:56,614
It hurts, Zura!

138
00:09:04,614 --> 00:09:05,614
Call, call!

139
00:09:10,614 --> 00:09:13,614
Hello, Krehi. Come here, won't you?

140
00:09:16,614 --> 00:09:17,614
My prince?

141
00:09:17,614 --> 00:09:19,614
Come, come now. Why the hunted look?

142
00:09:19,614 --> 00:09:22,414
Let's enjoy ourselves.

143
00:09:22,414 --> 00:09:25,414
I want to get all my feelings back, the sooner the better.

144
00:09:25,414 --> 00:09:29,414
Once that's taken care of, I can give the raven my heart.

145
00:09:29,414 --> 00:09:32,414
What are you saying? That's a joke, right?

146
00:09:32,414 --> 00:09:35,414
The prince is fated to marry no one but me.

147
00:09:35,414 --> 00:09:36,414
Marry you?

148
00:09:36,414 --> 00:09:41,414
You who, in spite of your being a crow, have that ugly human body.

149
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:43,414
That's the joke.

150
00:09:43,414 --> 00:09:46,414
The only thing that you are allowed to do is love me.

151
00:09:46,414 --> 00:09:49,414
The moment you died, you'll have to love me.

152
00:09:49,414 --> 00:09:52,214
You died my heart with raven's blood.

153
00:09:52,214 --> 00:09:55,214
Our fates were immediately sealed.

154
00:09:55,214 --> 00:09:58,214
But I did just what father told me to.

155
00:09:58,214 --> 00:10:02,214
Then I'd rather just take his heart out again.

156
00:10:02,214 --> 00:10:05,214
But I don't have the prince's sword.

157
00:10:05,214 --> 00:10:08,214
If I thrust this sword into the prince, he might die.

158
00:10:08,214 --> 00:10:10,014
That's fine.

159
00:10:10,014 --> 00:10:14,014
If that happens, I too will...

160
00:10:14,014 --> 00:10:20,014
I have one last favor to ask.

161
00:10:20,014 --> 00:10:22,014
After you've ripped out my heart,

162
00:10:22,014 --> 00:10:27,014
I want you to kiss it and dye your lips crimson with my blood.

163
00:10:27,014 --> 00:10:31,814
What's the matter?

164
00:10:31,814 --> 00:10:33,814
Can't you do it?

165
00:10:33,814 --> 00:10:39,814
Well, looks like you've reached your limit.

166
00:10:39,814 --> 00:10:44,814
I'll admit, picking Drosselmeyer's grave to write at was pretty sharp for you.

167
00:10:44,814 --> 00:10:49,614
But if the words you should be writing aren't coming to you without even having to think...

168
00:10:49,614 --> 00:10:51,614
Could you please be a little quieter?

169
00:10:51,614 --> 00:10:52,614
And think.

170
00:10:52,614 --> 00:10:56,614
At this moment, I have volumes upon volumes that I want to write.

171
00:10:56,614 --> 00:10:57,614
It's ironic.

172
00:10:57,614 --> 00:10:58,614
Faster.

173
00:10:58,614 --> 00:11:00,614
I've got to write faster.

174
00:11:00,614 --> 00:11:02,414
Good grief.

175
00:11:02,414 --> 00:11:06,414
You'd be better off letting the story pull you along like a good boy.

176
00:11:06,414 --> 00:11:09,414
Well, it's of no real consequence.

177
00:11:09,414 --> 00:11:11,414
You needn't fret, little duck.

178
00:11:11,414 --> 00:11:14,414
I'll be coming for you soon.

179
00:11:14,414 --> 00:11:43,214
I'll be coming for you soon.

180
00:11:43,214 --> 00:11:46,874
Who's there?

181
00:11:48,034 --> 00:11:52,914
Welcome to this quaint little gap in time, my dear Princess Tutu.

182
00:11:53,394 --> 00:11:54,654
Mr. Drosselmeyer.

183
00:11:55,114 --> 00:11:59,354
So, what did those puppets mean when they told me I stopped the story?

184
00:11:59,834 --> 00:12:00,654
I'm just...

185
00:12:00,654 --> 00:12:05,934
trying my best to completely return the prince's heart to it.

186
00:12:05,934 --> 00:12:10,034
Tell me, have you discovered all the locations of the scattered heart, Charles?

187
00:12:10,374 --> 00:12:10,694
What?

188
00:12:10,694 --> 00:12:15,154
Um, I'm not quite sure, but I think that they're hidden in the five gates around the town.

189
00:12:15,174 --> 00:12:17,034
My congratulations to you.

190
00:12:17,294 --> 00:12:17,654
What?

191
00:12:18,014 --> 00:12:22,534
So if I return those five shards to him, the prince will go back to normal and defeat the raven and then...

192
00:12:22,534 --> 00:12:23,654
No, no, no.

193
00:12:23,894 --> 00:12:25,694
That would be hopelessly boring.

194
00:12:26,434 --> 00:12:27,874
You're a story character.

195
00:12:28,114 --> 00:12:29,514
You can do better than that.

196
00:12:30,134 --> 00:12:30,614
Character?

197
00:12:31,234 --> 00:12:32,494
But how can that be?

198
00:12:32,574 --> 00:12:33,874
I'm really only a duck.

199
00:12:34,094 --> 00:12:34,454
Correct.

200
00:12:34,834 --> 00:12:37,074
But you're inside the story right now.

201
00:12:37,534 --> 00:12:38,574
Everybody is.

202
00:12:38,934 --> 00:12:39,774
Take a look.

203
00:12:40,694 --> 00:12:44,014
Rue.

204
00:12:45,474 --> 00:12:46,214
Fuck here.

205
00:12:47,574 --> 00:12:48,234
Mewtwo.

206
00:12:48,374 --> 00:12:50,394
Everyone's suffering, you see.

207
00:12:50,894 --> 00:12:52,654
This is the way it has to be.

208
00:12:53,114 --> 00:12:55,694
Tutu has something she should suffer over, too.

209
00:12:56,014 --> 00:12:58,934
The choice to confess her love and immediately vanish,

210
00:12:58,934 --> 00:13:03,294
or never to confess her love and thereby forever lose the prince.

211
00:13:03,714 --> 00:13:04,814
Never mind that.

212
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:10,234
And yet to think, returning the prince to normal is more important to you than your own problems.

213
00:13:10,234 --> 00:13:17,794
You're a much different duck now than the one you once were who so desired was for the prince.

214
00:13:17,794 --> 00:13:22,174
You should be desperately in love with the prince and want to marry him.

215
00:13:22,254 --> 00:13:23,014
Am I wrong?

216
00:13:23,014 --> 00:13:25,014
I just...

217
00:13:25,014 --> 00:13:26,054
That's right.

218
00:13:26,334 --> 00:13:28,634
You shouldn't fight what's natural.

219
00:13:28,634 --> 00:13:32,954
It's only natural to want to make the prince yours and yours alone.

220
00:13:32,954 --> 00:13:35,534
There's nothing to be shamed of.

221
00:13:35,974 --> 00:13:36,874
I know.

222
00:13:37,254 --> 00:13:39,074
How does this idea appeal to your nature?

223
00:13:39,414 --> 00:13:44,454
Simply pretend you haven't realized that the remaining heart shards are hidden in the five gates.

224
00:13:44,614 --> 00:13:44,894
What?

225
00:13:44,894 --> 00:13:48,134
After all, nobody else has realized.

226
00:13:48,334 --> 00:13:52,154
So if you do that, there will be nothing to part you from the prince.

227
00:13:52,814 --> 00:13:53,174
That...

228
00:13:53,174 --> 00:13:57,574
My dear duck, if you can't think, at least on that level, you'll never leave here.

229
00:13:57,714 --> 00:13:59,554
And the story will stay stopped, too.

230
00:14:02,694 --> 00:14:03,734
What's this?

231
00:14:04,014 --> 00:14:06,414
Tutu is here and yet the gears are moving.

232
00:14:06,834 --> 00:14:07,794
What is going on?

233
00:14:08,454 --> 00:14:09,634
Oh, no.

234
00:14:11,214 --> 00:14:11,734
Interesting.

235
00:14:12,314 --> 00:14:14,674
The gears are starting to turn backwards.

236
00:14:14,894 --> 00:14:17,714
The story will now double back on itself.

237
00:14:18,074 --> 00:14:18,494
What?

238
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:22,194
I never once envisioned something like this.

239
00:14:22,714 --> 00:14:23,414
How intriguing.

240
00:14:23,974 --> 00:14:25,614
I wonder what will happen.

241
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:31,234
I don't understand anymore.

242
00:14:31,874 --> 00:14:36,274
I believe that my marriage to the prince was the fate the story had decided for us.

243
00:14:37,274 --> 00:14:38,494
Was I wrong?

244
00:14:38,814 --> 00:14:40,214
What should I believe?

245
00:14:40,314 --> 00:14:41,594
Whom should I believe?

246
00:14:44,894 --> 00:14:49,074
I want to go back to that time before I remembered everything.

247
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:51,414
That time when I was Rue.

248
00:14:57,794 --> 00:14:58,974
Help me!

249
00:14:58,974 --> 00:15:07,154
I'm sorry, father.

250
00:15:08,154 --> 00:15:09,674
Don't take my heart.

251
00:15:09,794 --> 00:15:10,814
Forgive me.

252
00:15:14,314 --> 00:15:15,854
That was...

253
00:15:15,854 --> 00:15:17,414
Help me a good girl.

254
00:15:17,414 --> 00:15:17,514
Oh!

255
00:15:22,794 --> 00:15:24,314
Get behind me.

256
00:15:24,314 --> 00:15:43,594
That's the prince.

257
00:15:43,874 --> 00:15:45,334
Back when I first met him.

258
00:15:45,334 --> 00:15:51,154
You don't have to worry anymore.

259
00:16:03,154 --> 00:16:04,534
Does it hurt?

260
00:16:04,534 --> 00:16:09,634
I brought water.

261
00:16:09,634 --> 00:16:14,554
I brought water.

262
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:25,714
Thank you.

263
00:16:26,174 --> 00:16:27,514
I have to go.

264
00:16:27,774 --> 00:16:28,474
Go where?

265
00:16:28,894 --> 00:16:30,314
Back home to my father.

266
00:16:30,314 --> 00:16:31,974
Who are you?

267
00:16:32,474 --> 00:16:33,734
My name is...

268
